            <abstract>
                <p><quote>The Thirty-Third Miracle of our Father Takla Hāymānot. May his prayer and
                        his blessing be with his beloved Takla Hāymānot for ever and ever. Amen! And
                        similarly in another city they gave of the grain belonging to our father to
                        a certain mule, in order that he might eat a full meal, but the matter was
                        grievous to God, Who hath taught us that such animals have no understanding,
                        for the Prophet saith concerning them, "Be ye not like unto the horse and
                        mule which are without "understanding." And our father the holy man Takla
                        Hāymānot, the healer, also healed a man whose body was full of sores by
                        reason of the severity of his disease, and whose bones protruded through his
                        skin, and everyone saw that his whole body was a mass of corruption. May the
                        prayer and blessing be with his beloved Takla Hāymānot for ever and ever!
                        Amen.</quote> (<bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/8SCM474J"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Budge1906Taklahaymanot"/><title level="m">The Life of Takla Hâymânôt, in the version of Dabra Lîbanôs, and The Miracles of Takla Hâymânôt in the version of Dabra Lîbanôs, and The Book of the Riches of Kings</title><editor><forename>E. A. Wallis</forename><surname>Budge</surname></editor><pubPlace>London</pubPlace><publisher>Privately printed for Lady Meux</publisher><date>1906</date><biblScope unit="volume">I-II</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Budge1906Taklahaymanot</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Budge1906Taklahaymanot</note><citedRange unit="page">327–328</citedRange></bibl>)</p>
